From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] lxc.py: enable adb without auth and debuggable

On WhaleOS, we want ADB to be accessible without RSA key authentication
so that developers can connect via SSH tunnel + adb connect without
setting up adb key pairs. Also enable ro.debuggable=1 so standard
Android debug tooling works.

The container rootfs system/build.prop already sets ro.adb.secure=0 but
vendor/waydroid.prop overrides it to 1 at container start. This patch
removes that override so the system setting takes effect.

--- a/tools/helpers/lxc.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/lxc.py
@@ -250,9 +250,9 @@ def make_base_props(args):
     if not os.path.exists("/dev/ashmem"):
         props.append("sys.use_memfd=true")

-    # Added for security reasons
-    props.append("ro.adb.secure=1")
-    props.append("ro.debuggable=0")
+    # WhaleOS: allow adb without auth; adbd listens on TCP 5555
+    props.append("ro.adb.secure=0")
+    props.append("ro.debuggable=1")

     egl = tools.helpers.props.host_get(args, "ro.hardware.egl")
